shader-rosetta collects third-party shaders, so no single license covers the whole repository.

- A directory that carries its own LICENSE file is under that license, and so is everything below it.
  That includes our translations of the shaders it holds, which are derived works of them.
- Everything else (the tooling, the manifests, the documentation) is under the MIT License below.

The readme lists every source, its license, and the commit its files were taken from.

